		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Abstract"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD380301F5"
		    documentation 	
|Multiplication with an Integer Power of 2:	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0))
	    module     	"Component View::Group::HalfGroup"
	    quidu      	"36BB260803DD"
	    language   	"Java")
	(object Class "absHalfGroup"
	    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateFinalizer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateStaticInitializer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateInstanceInitializer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateDefaultConstructor"
		    value      	FALSE))
	    quid       	"36BB26160012"
	    documentation 	
|Default Implementation of an additive HalfGroup (G,+).
| * The Interface is separated out, because of Symmetry 
| * to the multiplicative HalfGroupM,
| * which  is used to simulate multiple Inheritance by Delegation. 
| * 
| * Design Decisions:
| * This class does not extend Number, because not every Realization of a Group 
| * maps to numeric Values. (e.g. Functions, Matrices etc.)
| * Also any other Argument Type than Object requires explicit casting on 
| * every Operation which is a hassle.
| * You can also not derive any of the helper Classes from Number, 
| * because you cannot cast between the branches, but you would have to
| * just to convert the results. So it is not possible!
| * 
| * It would have been much better, if the Java Group 
| * would have made 'Number' an Interface.
| * 
| * The Conflict culminates in Fraction which can contain
| * Numbers as well as any other Metric Integrity Ring. 
| * 
| * Instead it presents the conversion Routines xxxxValue(Object arg)
| * to convert from Number Types.
| * The conversion Routines are moved to countable and measurable.
| * 
| * Not all Methods are implemented as Defaults although that would be possible:
| * This is for one thing to keep this Class abstract 
| * and for another to indicate the Methods that have in any case to be redefined.
| * 
| * This abstract Class is not intended for Delegation. 
| * This leads to the following Design Decisions:
| * The Return Type is chosen to be absHalfGroup instead of HalfGroup,
| * because this saves a cast from other Interface Types on returning the Result.
| * The Execution is not delegated to a Self_ Variable.
| * 
| * Abstract Methods:
| * addAt (+=)
| 
	    
	    superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
		(object Inheritance_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD373B00A3"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::BaseCopy::absCopyAble"
		    quidu      	"36BB22B9029F"))
	    realized_interfaces 	(list realize_rel_list
		(object Realize_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD374002D1"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::Group::HalfGroup"
		    quidu      	"36BB260C00B8"))
	    operations 	(list Operations
		(object Operation "add"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD3746013F"
		    documentation 	
|Addition: +				
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "arg"
			    type       	"Object"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "dbl"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0385"
		    documentation 	
|Double:   2x == x+x		
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "dblAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0386"
		    documentation 	
|Double in Place: x+=x	
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "trpl"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0387"
		    documentation 	
|Triple: 3x == (2x)+=x	
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "trplAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C038F"
		    documentation 	
|Triple in Place: x+=2x	
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "quad"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0390"
		    documentation 	
|Quadruple: 4x == 2(2x)	
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "quadAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0391"
		    documentation 	
|Quadruple in Place: 2(2x)	
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mul2PowAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD375C0399"
		    documentation 	
|Multiplication with an Integer Power of 2 in Place:
|	 * Here implemented as a concatenated doubling.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mul2Pow"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD376C016B"
		    documentation 	
|Multiplication with an Integer Power of 2:
|	 * Here implemented as a concatenated doubling.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mul"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD377F037C"
		    documentation 	
|Integer Multiplication: x*n	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mulAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD379203BF"
		    documentation 	
|Integer Multiplication: x*=n
|	 * This Implementation is only valid for positive n > 0 !
|	 * You can implement a similar Algorithm for Multiplication.
|	 * This Algorithm uses the binary Representation of the integer n.
|	 * You could also write this with Prime Factors, but the Algorithm would be less
|	 * elegant and also slower, because this one uses only 2*lb n Multiplications.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroup"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "testIt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Static"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD37A90386"
		    documentation 	
|Method to test all Implementations in this class.
|	 * Must call testIt of the super Class.	 
		    
		    result     	"void"
		    exceptions 	"java.io.IOException"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0))
	    module     	"Component View::Group::absHalfGroup"
	    quidu      	"36BB261202FB"
	    language   	"Java"
	    abstract   	TRUE)
